h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 507)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>A review you're sent opens with the right color.</b> Packages built as HEVC or ProRes carry the display transform and the grade already in the picture, but the session that came with them still described the original render — so the transform was applied a second time on opening and the shots looked wrong. The package now describes what the file actually is, and it opens the way the person who sent it saw it.</li>
<li><b>Optimized bundles arrive complete.</b> Voice-note audio, A/B compare sides, the session gate and the loop scope now travel with the bundle, and a bundle containing a QuickTime no longer arrives with that clip pointing at a folder on someone else's machine.</li>
<li><b>Whole sequences arrive.</b> When a review comes from a conformed cut, the render travels with it rather than a single frame.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
